description: AquaWatch scope and honesty guardrails. Always applies.
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow `AGENTS.md` at the repo root. It defines the project's scope, its hard rules and when a task is done.

The short version:

- Work only on what the task asks, inside `src/`, `app.py`, `tests/`, `scripts/` and the docs listed in AGENTS.md.
- Ask the person before you:
  - add or upgrade a dependency
  - change CI
  - download anything
  - delete files
  - touch git history
  - add a new framework or service
- Never use `simulated_leak_label` or `simulated_event_id` in training. Never tune thresholds on the test window.
- Never write code that connects to or controls real utility systems. This project is read-only analytics on simulated data.
- Keep claims honest: an alert means "investigate", not "leak confirmed".
- Before you finish, run `python -m ruff check .` and `python -m pytest -q`, and report the results. Do not commit or push unless asked.
